{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\n\nThree repo gates are enforced by pytest but not by `make lint`, so the documented local\npre-flight returns green on a tree CI rejects:\n\n| gate | how it surfaced |\n|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` | change 2601 pushed red; `make lint` exit 0 |\n| `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` | change 2600 pushed red |\n| `tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py` | change 2609 pushed red; `make lint` exit 0 |\n\nAll three fired on 2026-09-04 on real changes whose authors had run `make lint` and\n`make typecheck` and seen them pass. The defect is the CONTRACT, not the placement: a\nproxy that returns green on a tree CI will reject turns \"I verified locally\" into a false\nstatement made in good faith.\n\nA survey of the test tree (recorded in a ticket comment) shows the class is not three\ntests but roughly seventy: ratchets, baselines, public-surface censuses, workflow-parity\nchecks, docs/registry drift gates and whole-tree AST policy scans. Any curated subset of\nthat is a second list to keep in sync -- the same drift defect one level up.\n\n## Approach\n\nDo not curate. `make test` already runs EXACTLY the marks CI's gating pytest leg runs:\n`DEFAULT_SUITE_MARKS` in `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` is\n`not integration and not external`, and `make test` is\n`pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"`. So the honest single command is the union\nof targets that already exist.\n\n1. **New `make verify` target = `lint typecheck test`** -- named in AGENTS.md as THE\n   pre-push contract. Complete by construction: no curated list, no new selection\n   mechanism, nothing to drift. It is a Makefile target, so it adds no `ci_gate` (that\n   kind is `scripts/check_*.py` files and workflow `run:` steps) and no other mechanism\n   kind -- the mechanism-delta ratchet sees no new entry.\n2. **`make lint`, `make typecheck` and the pre-commit hook are untouched.** They stay the\n   fast commit gate; the commit-time cost is unchanged.\n3. **`make check`'s help text stops over-claiming.** It reads \"Run every check-only gate\n   (no mutation)\" today and runs only `lint typecheck` -- part of how the false green got\n   its authority. It becomes an accurate description that points at `verify`.\n4. **`make test` gains `-n auto --dist worksteal`.** CI runs the suite under xdist and\n   local runs it serially; that is itself a local/CI divergence of the kind this bug is\n   about, and the repo already pins pytest-xdist in `[dev]` for scheduler parity. It also\n   keeps `make verify` inside a wall clock a contributor will actually pay.\n\nRejected: a curated `make check-gates` node list (a second list, drifts); a `repo_gate`\npytest marker (marker selection still pays a whole-tree collect, and marking ~70 modules\nleaves the same \"did you remember to mark it\" hole); folding pytest into `make lint`\n(breaks the commit hook's speed budget).\n\n## AC3 -- the `git add` skew\n\n`test_predates_gate_guard_parity._tracked_paths()` runs `git ls-files scripts tests docs\n.github`, so it cannot see a gate file that is written but not yet staged: the gate\nreports green before `git add` and red after, on the same working tree. It becomes\n`git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`, i.e. the tree as CI will see it once\ncommitted. The change is strictly widening -- every path it adds is one MORE step that\nmust carry a guard -- so it can only turn a false green red, never the reverse.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `make verify` exists and runs `lint`, `typecheck` and `test`; its help text names it\n      as the pre-push contract.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and `.pre-commit-config.yaml` are unchanged in scope,\n      so commit-time cost is unchanged.\n- [ ] `make check`'s help text no longer claims to run every check-only gate.\n- [ ] Introducing a violation of each of the three named gates in turn makes `make verify`\n      fail while `make lint` still exits 0; the three RED runs are quoted on the ticket.\n- [ ] `_tracked_paths()` includes untracked, non-ignored paths, so the parity gate's\n      verdict does not change when a new gate file is `git add`ed; a new regression test\n      pins that a written-but-unstaged path is seen.\n- [ ] AGENTS.md names `make verify` as the pre-push contract and `make lint` as the\n      commit-time gate, and says why `make lint` alone is not sufficient.\n- [ ] `docs/local-dev-env.md`'s \"Day-to-day gates\" block lists `make verify`.\n- [ ] `make verify` needs no CI provider -- make + ruff + mypy + pytest over the checkout\n      only (`project.portability`).\n- [ ] The measured wall-clock cost of `make verify` is recorded on the ticket, so the\n      \"slow enough to be skipped\" risk is evidenced rather than assumed.\n\n## Testing\n\nEvery command is run from this change's own worktree with its venv first on `PATH`\n(`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" <cmd>`).\n\n- `make lint` -- the unchanged commit gate is clean, and neither the complexity nor the\n  mechanism-delta ratchet fires on this change.\n- `make typecheck` -- mypy over `src/rebar` and `scripts/`.\n- `make verify` -- the new contract end to end on a clean tree, timed with `time`: passes.\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` -- the AC3 fix and its new\n  regression test.\n- Three RED demonstrations, each reverted immediately after, output quoted on the ticket:\n  1. add a stale entry to `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` -> `make verify` fails in\n     `test_mechanism_delta.py::test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree` while\n     `make lint` still exits 0;\n  2. drop one `[ -f ... ]` guard in `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` ->\n     `make verify` fails in `test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`;\n  3. add a symbol to `rebar.__all__` -> `make verify` fails in\n     `test_api_surface_gate.py` while `make lint` still exits 0.\n- The `git add` skew demonstration: write a new unguarded gate-script reference, run the\n  parity test before and after `git add`, and show the verdict is identical in both states\n  (on `main` it differs).\n\n## File impact\n\n`Makefile` (`verify`, `check` help text, `test` scheduler), `AGENTS.md` (the pre-push\ncontract), `docs/local-dev-env.md` (day-to-day gates),\n`tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` (AC3 + regression test)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788513594216409001,"uuid":"96c159e9-df94-4e55-b717-0102c6358f44"}